spoiler warning ahead for squid game  season one he's everyone's favorite  gamboo player one o il nam but behind  that old seemingly innocent facade is  what many have argued is a criminal  mastermind but i'm here to tell you  don't believe those lies player one did  nothing wrong in this video i'll be  laying out the case for why illness bad  rap is unwarranted and how his decisions  throughout the game even ones that lead  to murder are actually benevolent but  before we begin make sure to like and  subscribe and if you need a refresher on  the show check out my squid game ending  explained i should first mention that my  argument here isn't that illnom is  perfect far from it every human is  flawed and this is represented  throughout our colorful cast of  characters songwoo is arguably the worst  of the lot lying about knowing one of  the games in advance tricking ali with a  fake bag of rocks resulting in his death  and the icing on the cake throwing  someone off the glass bridge hell even  gyun exploits ilnam's quote-unquote  dementia to avoid defeat in the marvel  game what i'm getting at here is that  ilnam is far from the most evil  character on the show in fact he shows a  lot of remorse and compassion but more  on that in a bit as we find out in the  series final episode player 1 is the  founder of squid game a game in which  contestants battle for their lives for  prize money and here is the first reason  oil nom did nothing wrong the games are  voluntary unlike similar death style  games like battle royale alice in  borderland or even the hunger games  contestants are given the opportunity  not to play we see this with guillen  who's given a card to enter he doesn't  have to go he does it on his own free  will even when he gets to the games he  signs a waiver which is juxtaposed to  the one he signed under duress from a  thug he owed money to in episode 1. gyan  and the other contestants did everything  voluntarily also address the argument  they didn't know they might die in the  first game later on in the video and if  this wasn't enough there's rule number  three contestants can choose to end the  games if the majority of players agree  illnam actually becomes the deciding  vote in ending the game if he was some  bloodthirsty maniac he would never have  voted to end it that's because ilnam has  an unspoken moral code about how the  game should be run who should be able to  compete and when it comes to him as a  player minimally affecting the outcome  the game's contestants aren't chosen at  random illness actually wants those who  need the money to participate in fact  there is a screening process of sorts  done through men like this guy who we  see engage geon in a game of dakji this  ensures contestants who take part really  need that money and the prize money  along with how it is distributed is  equally noble as we learn in episode 2  the total prize pool is 45.6 billion won  or roughly 38 and a half million us  dollars that's more than enough to  change someone's life and no matter the  outcome of the game money will be given  out if for example the contestants  decide to end the game the families of  the deceased will be given a hundred  million won illnom doesn't have to do  that but he does even though these  contestants voluntarily chose to be here  players are even given the chance to  come back to the games knowing it could  result in their deaths episode 2 is  titled hell and shows us the backstory  of several of these characters for them  life in the outside world is more of a  hell than playing the actual game ilnam  is merely giving them an opportunity  under their own volition to change the  course of their lives in a world which  has been so unfair to them but what sets  ilnam apart is that he actually plays  the game he puts his own life at risk in  order to play now i've seen a few  articles about how illnom supposedly had  the doll in the red light green light  game programmed so that it wouldn't kill  him i don't believe this for a few  reasons i went back and watched the  scene multiple times and you can clearly  see that illness does get scanned and  there are no indications that he moves  while on red light which would have  resulted in his death but i think the  point at which illness could have easily  died was the tug of war game his team  was clearly outmatched in strength and  even with his technique they used to win  the game they barely win if illness was  rigging these games to win this was  definitely not the play but for ilnam  it's not about winning he actually exits  the game after faking his death in  episode 6. in episode three illness even  thanks guyan for showing him the licking  technique in the honeycomb challenge  plus illness could have chosen the easy  triangle shape but went with the star  this is a guy who isn't afraid of a  challenge but perhaps the strongest  evidence that he didn't rig the red  light greenlight game is that it would  take the fun out of it on his deathbed  illness talks about the reason for both  starting the games and participating in  them fun as an extremely rich man  illness felt that nothing in life was  fun anymore there was no challenge no  fight nothing if he wanted something he  could easily buy it he has this great  line where he says the one thing that  extremely poor and extremely rich people  have in common is that for both of them  life is not fun if ilnam rigged the  games it would take away that fun  there's no fun in winning a game you  know you're going to win also if there  was no chance of death for him illness  would have risked exposing himself to  the other players there are also  multiple times in the show where the  front man espouses the virtues of having  fair and equal games so when it's  discovered that one of the contestants  has been given secret information about  the upcoming game that player is  eliminated during episode 4 it is ilnam  who stops the riot from killing everyone  in the dormitory while this massacre is  going on these soldiers merely wait for  instructions letting the killing  continue but it's only when illness  screams out for the killing to stop that  frontman sends in the army i personally  think this is because illness believes  this is not what the games are about we  can see him visibly upset in the  aftermath he even agrees to keep  nightwatch for his team in the aftermath  should another attack happen ilnam also  forges a relationship with gyan  something he probably shouldn't have  done if he generally wanted to see these  players killed in episode two when  they're in the outside world illnom  happens to show up where gian is and  even shares a pack of noodles with him  what a sweetheart and two episodes later  ilnam shows compassion while gion  recounts the story of his friend at the  car plant being murdered by police what  i'm getting at here is that ilnam isn't  the soulless character that a show like  this could have easily portrayed him as  there is humanity to him and this is  shaped by a moral code that acts as the  backbone to the games but the connection  between these two players really shines  in episode 6 gambu a korean slang word  roughly meaning friendship ilnam ends up  giving his player jacket to gyun after  gyun gave his own to cover up his pants  he lets geon win the marble game even  though gyun tried to exploit his  dementia in essence ilnom forgives him  here a forgiveness and compassion given  to gion based on the kindness he showed  him throughout the series and for quote  giving him a good experience the last  episode however is where we get the most  insight into who ilnam really is this  provides the backstory for why he  created the games and additional insight  into his worldview illnon believes we  make our own choices just like the drunk  man outside who chose to drink and  nearly kills himself in the cold he so  believes that humanity is not good that  he bets gion his life that no one will  help the drunk man and this in my  opinion is his biggest flaw he simply  has a misguided view of humanity it's  partially why he doesn't feel any guilt  for the thousands of contestants killed  over the years they chose to be there  they chose money over life so who is  really to blame in this twisted game the  man who created it or the contestants  who willfully choose to play it should  the drunk man blame the alcohol or  himself for choosing to drink it you can  see how it gets a bit more complex here  there's also this beautiful irony  between ilnam and the drunk man a man  who is literally sitting and dying  juxtaposed with what ilnam says in  episode 2.  now the main argument of this video is  that ilnam did nothing wrong and you  could say that he is the one responsible  for all these deaths but at the end of  the day the contestants voluntarily  chose to take that risk and you might  say well they didn't know they'd die in  the first round but they were expressly  told that if they follow the rules they  would not be harmed so those who didn't  follow the rules i.e moved during the  red light game were killed and any  liability toward illness would be  negated because of the player consent  forms a consent form which clearly  states in rule 2 that players who refuse  to play will be eliminated any of the  contestants could have specifically  asked what eliminated meant but none of  them do the real gray areas here that  i'm sure i'm gonna hear about in the  comments will likely fall on our own  subjective opinions on what is right and  wrong and that's the fun of these types  of videos one man's right is the other  man's wrong but i want to hear what you  think am i totally off here and illnom  is evil incarnate or is there a  different way of looking at things  remember all of you are my gambu and  please be kind to each other in the  comments thanks for watching everyone be  sure to like and subscribe and for more  bad takes you can follow me on twitter  and instagram at thingstoryt until next  time remember daddy loves you very much

